        "id": 1836235
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-29T15:01:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m generally taking the approach that if the text of the AIDL spec mandates something, we should have a test for it (for this one it says \"If provided with a non-prime value, generateKey must return ErrorCode::INVALID_ARGUMENT.\").\n\nI guess the alternative is to remove that text from the AIDL spec.",
      "parentUuid": "57e8e3e5_d8a1388f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 962,
        "startChar": 49,
        "endLine": 962,
        "endChar": 81
      },
      "revId": "ff5a9229cb649520e2e15c149c6d0e9cc6fff11c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "59771f19_8260524f",
        "filename": "security/keymint/aidl/vts/functional/KeyMintTest.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 962,
      "author": {
        "id": 1043663
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-30T14:43:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "After discussion and reflection, I think we should remove it from the spec.  It\u0027s obviously a very bad idea to use non-prime values, but I hate to burden implementations with a primality test (even if just in the HAL).\n\nI guess it\u0027s also not technically true that non-primes are disallowed for security; IIRC you just need e to be coprime with λ(n), where λ is somebody\u0027t totient function, and a trivial way to ensure that for all n is to choose a prime e.  A really proper test would probably try to see if it\u0027s possible to create a key (probably by importing) s.t. e and λ(n) have a common factor.\n\nThis is all kind of pointless, though, everyone should just use F4, which is the default.  Anyone choosing to override the default had better know what they\u0027re doing and why.",
      "parentUuid": "86fadbbc_113292bd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 962,
        "startChar": 49,
        "endLine": 962,
        "endChar": 81
      },
      "revId": "ff5a9229cb649520e2e15c149c6d0e9cc6fff11c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
